title: "pallet-multi-asset-bounties: refund parent bounty net of paid-out child-bounty value on close"
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    `close_bounty` on a parent bounty refunded the full stored `value` to the funding source,
    ignoring the value of its paid-out child-bounties (`ChildBountiesValuePerParent`). Since that
    value has already left the parent bounty account, the refund over-requested and, with a
    paymaster that performs a real transfer (e.g. `LocalPay`), failed with `RefundError` on every
    attempt. Governance could therefore never close such a parent bounty and reclaim its remaining
    funds through the intended path.

    The refund path now uses the same `calculate_payout` adjustment as the payout path, so the
    parent bounty refunds `value - ChildBountiesValuePerParent`, i.e. exactly what it holds.
    Child-bounty refunds are unchanged.
crates:
- name: pallet-multi-asset-bounties
  bump: patch
